Creating a simple website involves several steps, from planning and designing to building and publishing. In this example, we'll create a one-page website with a few sections: a header, a main content area, and a footer. I'll provide a simple HTML, CSS, and a little bit of JavaScript code for this purpose.

**Step 1: Plan your website**

Before starting, decide what your website will look like and what content it will include. For our simple website, we'll have the following sections:

1. Header: Logo and navigation menu
2. Main content area: A big "Hello, world!" heading and a paragraph
3. Footer: Copyright information

**Step 2: Create the HTML structure**
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <title>Simple Website</title>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <!-- Add your logo and navigation menu here -->
  </header>
  <main>
    <section>
      <h1>Hello, world!</h1>
      <p>This is a simple website for demonstration purposes.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <p>Simple Website &copy; 2023. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
```
**Step 3: Style your website with CSS**

Create a `styles.css` file and add the following styles:
```css
/* General reset */
* {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Header styles */
header {
  background-color: #333;
  color: #fff;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 1rem;
}

/* Main content styles */
main {
  padding: 2rem;
}

h1 {
  font-size: 3rem;
  font-weight: bold;
}

p {
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

/* Footer styles */
footer {
  background-color: #333;
  color: #fff;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 1rem;
}
```
**Step 4: Add some JavaScript (Optional)**

If you want to add some interactivity, you can include a bit of JavaScript code in your ` `<header>`` or ` `<footer>`` section. For example, you can create a simple scrolling effect when the user scrolls down the page:
```html
<!-- Add this script in the header or footer section -->
<script>
  window.addEventListener('scroll', function() {
    let header = document.querySelector('header');
    let scrollingDown = window.pageYOffset > document.querySelector('header').offsetHeight;

    header.classList.toggle('scrolled', scrollingDown);
  });
</script>
```
Now add the `scrolling` class in your `styles.css`:
```css
header {
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
}

header.scrolled {
  transform: translateY(-100%);
}
```
This code snippet adds a smooth scrolling effect to the header when the user scrolls down the page.

**Step 5: Put it all together**

Combine the HTML code, CSS, and JavaScript into a single file or separate them into their respective files (`index.html`, `styles.css`, and `scripts.js`).

Upload the files to a web server or use a service like GitHub Pages, Netlify, or Vercel to host your website. Open the website in a web browser to see your simple website in action.

