To disable entering full screen mode on mobile devices in a React project using the react-player library, you can achieve this by defining custom config options for the specific players that react-player supports (e.g., YouTube, Vimeo, etc.), and using those options in conjunction with the ReactPlayer component.

Here's an example of how you can achieve this with a YouTube player:

1. Install the `react-player` package if you haven't:

```bash
npm install react-player
```

2. In your component file, import `ReactPlayer` and set up the config options:

```javascript
import React from 'react'
import ReactPlayer from 'react-player'

const CustomReactPlayer = () => {
    // Define player configurations
    const playerConfig = {
        youtube: {
            playerVars: {
                fs: 0 // Disabling the full screen button for YouTube
            }
        },
        vimeo: {
            playerOptions: {
                fullscreen: 0 // Disable full screen for Vimeo
            }
        } // Add desired configurations for other players
    }

    return (
        <div>
            <ReactPlayer
                url="https://youtu.be/your-video-url" // Replace with your video URL
                config={playerConfig}
            />
        </div>
    )
}

export default CustomReactPlayer;
```

Please replace "`https://youtu.be/your-video-url`" with the actual YouTube video URL you want to embed. This configuration will ensure that the full screen button is disabled for mobile devices.

For more players and configurations, check the react-player documentation: https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-player

Remember that completely disabling full-screen mode might be against the user's wishes. An alternative solution is to implement custom player controls, allowing the user to decide whether they want to use full-screen mode.

