To translate a sentence using JavaScript, you can use an API like Google Translate. The Google Translate API has been deprecated, but you can still use it for non-commercial purposes with a custom API key. First, follow these steps to get a custom API key:

1. Visit the Google Cloud Platform Console: <https://console.cloud.google.com/>
2. Sign in with your Google account, or create a new account if you don't have one.
3. Create a new project by clicking on the "+" icon in the top right corner and selecting "Create a new project."
4. In your new project dashboard, click on "Enable APIs and Services."
5. In the API Library, search for "Google Translate API" and click on the first result.
6. Click "Enable" to enable the API for your project.
7. Click "Create credentials" in the top right corner and select "API key" to create an API key.

Once you have your API key, you can use the following code to translate the sentence "Je veux aller au marché" into English:
```javascript
const translate = 'translate.google.com/translate_a/t'; // Updated!
const key = 'YOUR_API_KEY'; // Replace with your API key
const sourceLanguage = 'fr'; // French
const targetLanguage = 'en'; // English
const sentence = 'Je veux aller au marché';

const translatedSentence = new Promise((resolve) => {
  fetch(`${translate}?sl=${sourceLanguage}&tl=${targetLanguage}&q=${encodeURIComponent(sentence)}&key=${key}`).then((response) => {
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error('Failed to fetch translation');
    }
    return response.text();
  }).then((translation) => {
    resolve(translation);
  });
});

translatedSentence.then((translation) => {
  console.log(translation); // Log the translated sentence
  document.getElementById('translation').innerHTML = translation; // Update the span element with the translated sentence
});
```
Remember to replace `'YOUR_API_KEY'` with your actual API key. This code fetches the translation using the Google Translate API, logs the translation to the console, and updates a span element with the ID `translation` on the page with the translated sentence.

Please note that Google Translate API usage is limited to 1000 translations per day for non-commercial purposes. For more usage or commercial purposes, you'll need to consider using the paid version of the API.

